{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user initiated a cobbler-scaffold \"stitch\" task (#5624) on branch `task/generation-run44-5624` for the go-unix-utils project. This is an automated code generation pipeline task. The specific work is to implement SRD 109 (dircolors utility) requirements R3.4 and R3.5. The requirement_states in the prompt confirm that `srd109-dircolors` R3.4 and R3.5 have status \"ready\" (need implementation). The acceptance criteria require: successful compilation, `go vet` passing, `go test` passing, differential test cases for R3.4 and R3.5, and all 15 srd109 requirements (R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.5, R3.1-R3.5) being implemented and tested.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementations of GNU coreutils verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries\n   - `dircolors` utility: outputs shell commands to set LS_COLORS for colorized ls output (GNU reference binary: `gdircolors`)\n   - Differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary vs GNU reference binary\n   - SIGPIPE handler requirement for all cmd/ utilities that write to stdout\n   - Cobbler-scaffold pipeline: measure (task planning) → stitch (code generation)\n   - Git is managed externally by the orchestrator - NO git commands allowed\n   - All files must start with SPDX copyright header\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max (hard limit per execution constitution E8)\n   - File size limit: 500 lines per Go source file\n   - Build output must go to `bin/` directory: `go build -o bin/<name> ./cmd/<name>/`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (provided in prompt)\n     - Contains the DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests function used for all differential testing\n     -